        "kdf_nh": 32,
        "aead_nk": 16,
        "aead_profile": "MLS_128_DHKEMX25519_AES128GCM_SHA256_Ed25519"
      },
      "expected": {
        "history_secret_hex": "c23c438ea6324409174e5fe5c330199fe511c44eca88f0100cc40eca29a84d2a",
        "content_expand_with_label_info_hex": "0010154d4c5320312e3020616b2e636f6e74656e742d763100",
        "content_key_hex": "86fe11a399474afc8d9a81b2f5a961bf"
      },
      "note": "aead_nk is AEAD.Nk of the ciphersuite the group actually negotiated, per encryption-and-audit.md 2.10.1, and 2.10.2 requires aead_profile to be an ACTIVE canonical_id of mls-ciphersuite-registry.json. The only active row is AES-128-GCM, so Nk is 16. The length is an ExpandWithLabel input, so a 16-byte key is not a prefix of a 32-byte one - an implementation following the normative text can never reproduce the latter."
    },
